  "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ has more than three divisors.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is composite.\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)\u21d2Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n\u00acP(x)\u2228Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $\u00acP(x):$ $x$ doesn't have more than three divisors.\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ doesn't have more than three divisors, or $x$ is composite.",
